Class: IntegerPairFinder

Method: findMaxXOR

Parameters:
 - nums: A 0-indexed integer array

Return type: Long: maxxor (representing the maximum XOR value from strong pairs)

Example:

  IntegerPairFinder finder = new IntegerPairFinder();
  int[] nums = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
  long maxxor = finder.findMaxXOR(nums); // Return: 7

  int[] nums = {10, 100};
  long maxxor = finder.findMaxXOR(nums); // Return: 0

  int[] nums = {500, 520, 2500, 3000};
  long maxxor = finder.findMaxXOR(nums); // Return: 1020

Note:

  The function findMaxXOR may raise an exception if the array nums is empty.
  The time complexity is expected to be O(n^2) in the worst case where n is the number of elements in nums, and the space complexity is expected to be O(n).
 */

public class IntegerPairFinder {

    public long findMaxXOR(int[] nums) {
        if (nums == null || nums.length == 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Array must not be empty");
        }

        // Placeholder for the result, starting with the smallest possible XOR value 0
        long maxxor = 0;

        // Sort the array to use two-pointer technique
        Arrays.sort(nums);

        // Use two-pointer technique to find maximum XOR from all pairs
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            long currentXOR = nums[i];
            for (int j = i + 1; j < nums.length; j++) {
                // Check the condition for a strong pair and find maxXOR for this strongly pair pair
                if (Math.abs(nums[i] - nums[j]) <= Math.max(nums[i], nums[j])) {
                    currentXOR = currentXOR ^ nums[j];
                }
                // Update the overall maxxor if we found a new maxXOR
                maxxor = Math.max(maxxor, currentXOR);
            }
            // When i reaches the middle because of the sorted array, remove the duplicates
            if (i == nums.length / 2)
                break;
        }

        return maxxor;
    }
}

